{{!--
AGENTS.hbs — personal global rules template for the Zed agent.

When this file exists and renders successfully, its output replaces the
verbatim `AGENTS.md` injection in the agent's system prompt. On a render
error Zed falls back to `AGENTS.md` and shows a warning. Delete this file
to return to plain `AGENTS.md` behavior entirely.

Text is emitted verbatim; comments like this one are stripped at render
time and never reach the model. For template syntax and the built-in
helpers see https://docs.rs/handlebars/latest/handlebars/#built-in-helpers

Zed renders in strict mode: an unknown variable fails the render, so a typo'd
name falls back to `AGENTS.md` with a warning rather than emitting nothing.

Context variables:
  available_tools   names of the tools enabled for this session
  model_name        active model name, if any
  date              today's date, YYYY-MM-DD
  is_windows        host platform gates
  is_linux
  is_macos
  sandboxing        whether terminal commands run in the OS-level sandbox

Zed registers one custom helper, `contains` (list, item):

  {{#if (contains available_tools 'grep')}}
  Prefer the `grep` tool for content search.
  {{/if}}

Partials (imports): `{{> agents_md}}` splices your `AGENTS.md` in place.
Every other `*.hbs` file under this directory (recursively) is importable by
its relative path without the extension, `/`-separated on every platform —
`partials/style.hbs` → `{{> partials/style}}`. Use `/` even on Windows:
`\` is the template escape character and cannot appear in a partial name.
--}}
{{> agents_md}}
